# What this repository publishes, and what it keeps local
#
# Tracked: code, configs, documentation, and small derived evidence produced by
# our own code.
# Not tracked: raw market data, downloaded third-party source material, and
# heavy regenerable run outputs.
#
# `docs/evidence-policy.md` states the rule and classifies every candidate.
# This file is only its mechanical form.
#
# Order matters here. A later line overrides an earlier one, and git never
# descends into a directory it has excluded, so every carve-out below first
# re-includes a directory and only then re-excludes the heavy files inside it.

# --- Python, packaging, local environment ----------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.env
monitor.env
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.claude/worktrees/

# --- Research data: local only ---------------------------------------------
# The sealed baseline contract sets redistribute_raw_data = false and
# local_research_only = true, so no vendor price or yield series is published
# here. The tracked route to rebuilding them is scripts/data/ plus the
# INPUT_SHA256 pins inside it; see data/README.md for what that route does and
# does not give a fresh clone.
data/*.tar.zst
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
data/external/*
# Cold storage for retired minute-era data (paid vendor).
data/legacy-cold/
# Exceptions: primary-source paper text/PDFs that are (a) load-bearing for
# [line NNN] citations elsewhere in the repo (check_paper_claims.py) and/or
# (b) freely redistributable arXiv preprints -- these must survive a lost
# local disk, unlike the bulk re-fetchable market-data CSVs this rule exists
# for. Paywalled/uncertain-license items (SSRN PDFs, the Princeton
# dissertation, slide decks) stay local-only.
!data/external/inputs/
data/external/inputs/*
!data/external/inputs/2402.05272v3.pdf
!data/external/inputs/shu_paper.txt
!data/external/inputs/shu-yu-mulvey-2406.09578.pdf
!data/external/inputs/shu-yu-mulvey-2406.09578.txt
!data/external/inputs/shu-mulvey-2410.14841.pdf
!data/external/inputs/shu-mulvey-2410.14841.txt

# --- Generated run outputs: local by default -------------------------------
artifacts/*

# Committed evidence. Small derived tables that a durable claim in README.md,
# CURRENT.md, docs/ or the manuscript depends on. Nothing heavy goes here and
# nothing here is read by the pipeline, so this directory needs no re-exclusion
# and new evidence belongs in it rather than as another carve-out below.
!artifacts/evidence/
# ...but never the heavy, regenerable kinds, even if someone copies them in.
artifacts/evidence/**/*.npz
artifacts/evidence/**/*.npy
artifacts/evidence/**/*.pkl
artifacts/evidence/**/*states*.csv
artifacts/evidence/**/features*.csv
artifacts/evidence/**/trades*.csv
artifacts/evidence/**/candidate-returns*.csv

# Per-study carve-outs, kept in the order they were added. Each one tracks a
# study's small tables and re-excludes its regenerable state matrices and
# numerical caches.
!artifacts/jm-residual/
artifacts/jm-residual/*/*-states.csv
artifacts/jm-residual/*/*/*-states.csv
artifacts/jm-residual/*/*/union-refits.csv
artifacts/jm-residual/*/*.npz
artifacts/jm-residual/*/*.npy
# Audit evidence: small tables and the scripts that produced them stay
# investigable; the refitted state matrices are regenerable and stay out.
!artifacts/audit/
artifacts/audit/*/states-*.csv
# lagged-capguard-001: readouts, metrics, choices and trades are committed
# evidence; regenerable daily state matrices would be the only heavy files
# and the runner does not persist them.
!artifacts/lagged-capguard/
# grid-selection-rule-001: per-market grid rankings are small committed
# evidence (a few hundred to tens of thousands of text rows); regenerable
# from the -008/-009 caches, which stay excluded above.
!artifacts/grid-selection-rule/
# v12 stress gate: 255-row objective comparison + verdict -- small committed
# evidence; the n_init=180 refits themselves are regenerable and not persisted.
!artifacts/v12-stress-gate/
# optimizer-fidelity characterization: the ladder tables are small committed
# evidence; the per-seed refit cache is regenerable and stays out.
!artifacts/optimizer-fidelity/
artifacts/optimizer-fidelity/fit-cache/
# confirmed_2d episode-level evidence: 27/55/49 one-row-per-episode tables.
!artifacts/confirmed2d-episodes/
# Track lightweight HMM audit evidence; keep state matrices and numerical caches local.
!artifacts/hmm-residual/
artifacts/hmm-residual/**/*states*.csv
artifacts/hmm-residual/**/*.npz
artifacts/hmm-residual/**/*.npy

# --- Third-party material we may not redistribute --------------------------
# Paywalled PDFs the owner downloaded via institutional SSRN access into
# paper/ for reading -- unlike arXiv preprints, SSRN's terms do not grant
# redistribution, so these stay local-only. paper/*.pdf that IS this project's
# own manuscript output (now under archive/paper/) is unaffected -- this lists
# exact filenames, not a blanket paper/*.pdf rule.
paper/s10479-026-07041-z.pdf
paper/ssrn-4556048.pdf
paper/ssrn-5235747.pdf
paper/ssrn-5817083.pdf
paper/ssrn-6933278.pdf

# --- Rendered pages, logs, databases, model weights ------------------------
# Rendered figure pages. The archived copies of the two HTML deliverables live
# in archive/docs/. Only the atlas carries a successful verifier certification;
# the capguard verifier still fails its frozen spec-hash gate, so that page is
# an archived copy of an unverified diagnosis. These paths are where the
# archived renderers in archive/scripts/rendering/ rewrite them.
docs/atlas/
docs/capguard-diagnosis/
reports/
*.log
*.pid
*.sqlite*
*.db
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
